# Installed dependencies — reproducible from the committed lockfiles.
node_modules/

# ...except this one, which is not a dependency tree at all. The browser-history
# demo ships a FAKE node_modules directory as static assets, served over HTTP to
# price Node's resolution algorithm against network latency. Without it, demo
# page 5 404s and measures nothing.
!modules/1-foundations-node-module-system/demos/1.1-browser-module-history/public/simulate/node_modules/

# Compiled output from the demos' `build` script.
dist/

# tsc incremental / build-mode state.
*.tsbuildinfo

# NOTE: pnpm-lock.yaml is deliberately NOT ignored.
# Lockfiles are the whole point of deterministic installs (lesson 1.5) — a demo
# whose lockfile is missing is a demo that can drift out from under you.

.DS_Store

# ...and these, which are the exercise fixtures for lesson 1.2 (the resolution
# algorithm). Hand-made trees with real `node_modules` directories, because the
# exercise IS predicting what Node finds in them. Nothing to install; do not run
# a package manager inside them.
